.\" lb-b4p
.\" Manual page for LazyBeads.
.TH LB 1 "2026-09-11" "LazyBeads @VERSION@" "LazyBeads Manual"
.nh
.ad l
.
.SH NAME
lb \- terminal operator console for Beads issue tracking
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lb
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B lb
.RI [ global-options ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B LazyBeads
is a read-first console over
.BR bd (1),
the Beads issue tracker. It helps an operator find the highest-leverage ready
task, understand why that task is ready, and act on it without losing the
audit trail.
.PP
.B lb
never talks to a database directly. Every read and every mutation is a
subprocess call to
.BR bd ,
executed as an argument vector with no shell interpolation. Anything
.B bd
cannot do,
.B lb
does not do either.
.PP
Invoked with no command on an interactive terminal,
.B lb
starts the full-screen interface described under
.BR "INTERACTIVE INTERFACE" .
With a command, or when standard input or output is not a terminal, it behaves
as an ordinary non-interactive tool: one shot, a stable exit code, and
optionally a versioned JSON envelope.
.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These flags are accepted by every command.
.
.SS Output
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the stable JSON envelope described under
.BR "JSON OUTPUT" .
Equivalent to
.BR "\-\-format json" ,
and it overrides
.BR \-\-format .
.TP
.BI \-\-format " format"
One of
.BR human " (default), " json ", or " jsonl
.RB ( ndjson
is accepted as a synonym, and
.B text
as a synonym for
.BR human ).
.B \-\-format yaml
is rejected with a usage error; YAML is not implemented.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " mode"
One of
.BR auto " (default), " always ", or " never .
Unset, the value falls back to
.B general.color
in configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Same as
.BR "\-\-color never" .
Takes precedence over
.BR \-\-color .
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Use ASCII glyphs instead of Unicode box drawing and status symbols. Implied by
.B tui.ascii
in configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress secondary commentary: notes, hints, and progress. Errors are still
printed.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Include upstream diagnostic detail. On failure this prints the captured
.B bd
stderr; on
.B lb next
it shows the full scoring breakdown.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Trace every
.B bd
invocation to stderr with secrets redacted, including argument vector, exit
code, and duration.
.
.SS Workspace selection
.TP
.BI \-\-project " path"
Resolve the Beads workspace starting from this repository path instead of the
current working directory. This also selects which
.B .lazybeads.toml
is discovered.
.TP
.BI \-\-beads\-dir " path"
Use this Beads directory explicitly, skipping discovery.
.TP
.BI \-\-rig " name"
Select a named rig for cross-rig operation.
.TP
.BI \-\-actor " identity"
Operator identity recorded on mutations and used by
.BR "\-\-assignee me" .
See
.BR "ACTOR IDENTITY" .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " duration"
Maximum wall-clock time for a single
.B bd
invocation, for example
.BR 30s .
See
.BR "DURATION SYNTAX" .
The default is 30 seconds.
.
.SS Mutation safety
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the interactive confirmation prompt. Required for any mutation in a
non-interactive context; without it
.B lb
refuses to mutate rather than assuming consent.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the
.B bd
argument vector that would be executed and exit without running it. Implies no
confirmation prompt and no mutation.
.
.SS Informational
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the LazyBeads version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage for the command and exit.
.
.SH COMMANDS
.
.SS Overview and discovery
.TP
.B lb status
Workspace health and work-state overview: ready, in-progress, and blocked
counts, the resolved workspace and actor, and any health checks that are not
.BR ok .
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-watch " duration"
Re-render on an interval, for example
.BR 5s .
Runs until interrupted.
.RE
.TP
.B lb ready
Unblocked work, ranked for an operator.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-priority\-max " n"
Keep issues at priority
.I n
or more urgent. Default 4 (everything).
.TP
.BI \-\-label " name"
Require this label. Repeat to require all of them (AND).
.TP
.BI \-\-parent " id"
Restrict to children of this issue.
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " key"
One of
.BR priority " (default), " leverage ", or " age .
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " n"
Maximum issues to print. 0 means no limit.
.RE
.TP
.B lb next
Recommend the highest-leverage ready task and explain the factors behind the
score. Every contributing factor is named; nothing influences a recommendation
invisibly. Use
.B \-\-verbose
for the full breakdown.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-strategy " name"
One of
.BR priority ", " leverage ", " age ", " balanced ", or " random .
Defaults to
.B ranking.strategy
in configuration
.RB ( balanced ).
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " n"
How many ranked tasks to show. Default 1; the rest are reported as
alternatives.
.TP
.BI \-\-parent " id"
Restrict recommendations to this epic or parent.
.RE
.TP
.BI "lb show" " id"
Render one issue in an action-oriented format: identity, status, priority,
assignee, blockers, dependents, and description.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-events
Include recent history inferred from the underlying commits.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Print the upstream JSON payload exactly as
.B bd
returned it, bypassing LazyBeads rendering.
.RE
.TP
.B lb list
Filter issues with Beads-compatible constraints.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-status " status"
Filter by status:
.BR open ", " in_progress ", " blocked ", " deferred ", " closed .
.TP
.BI \-\-type " type"
Filter by issue type, for example
.BR task ", " bug ", " feature ", " epic .
.TP
.BI \-\-label " name"
Require this label. Repeat to require all of them (AND).
.TP
.BI \-\-label\-any " name"
Match any of these labels (OR). Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-assignee " actor"
Filter by assignee. The literal
.B me
resolves to the current actor and fails with a usage error if no actor is
configured.
.TP
.BI \-\-query " text"
Local full-text filter applied after Beads returns candidates.
.TP
.BI \-\-created\-after " time"
Keep issues created after this time.
.TP
.BI \-\-updated\-before " time"
Keep issues updated before this time.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Disable the default safety limit and include closed work.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " n"
Maximum issues to print.
.RE
.TP
.BI "lb search" " query..."
Fuzzy discovery across issue identity, title, description, and labels. All
arguments are joined with spaces into one query.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Include closed issues.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " n"
Maximum results. Default 20.
.RE
.
.SS Explanation and graph
.TP
.BI "lb why" " id"
Explain why an issue is ready or blocked, naming the specific unresolved
blockers and the path to each.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " n"
Traversal depth. 0 uses
.B ranking.max_graph_depth
from configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-paths
Keep every path through a cycle instead of collapsing to the first.
.RE
.TP
.BI "lb graph" " id"
Render a dependency graph rooted at an issue.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-direction " dir"
One of
.BR blockers ", " dependents ", or " both " (default)."
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " n"
Traversal depth. 0 uses the configured default.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " form"
One of
.BR tree " (default), " dot ", or " json .
This is separate from the global
.BR \-\-format ;
.B dot
emits Graphviz source suitable for piping to
.BR dot (1).
.RE
.TP
.B lb blocked
Blocked work grouped by its closest unresolved blocker, so a single fix that
unblocks many issues is visible as one group.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-priority\-max " n"
Keep this priority or more urgent.
.TP
.BI \-\-group\-by " key"
.BR blocker " (default) or " parent .
.RE
.
.SS Operator views
.TP
.B lb focus
Work most relevant to the current operator: issues you have claimed, plus work
you have recently touched.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-all\-actors
Include every actor's claimed work, not only your own.
.TP
.BI \-\-recent " duration"
Recently-touched window. Default
.BR 24h .
Accepts
.B today
as well as a duration.
.RE
.TP
.B lb stale
Surface quiet in-progress claims: work that is claimed but has not moved.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-since " duration"
Idle threshold. Defaults to
.B general.stale_after
from configuration (8h). Accepts
.BR today .
.TP
.BI \-\-priority\-max " n"
Keep this priority or more urgent.
.TP
.B \-\-claimed\-only
Only issues that actually have an assignee.
.RE
.TP
.B lb activity
Operational event feed inferred from the underlying commit history.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-since " duration"
How far back to look. Default
.BR 24h ;
.B today
is accepted.
.TP
.BI \-\-issue " id"
Restrict to one issue.
.TP
.BI \-\-actor " identity"
Restrict to one actor.
.TP
.BI \-\-type " kind"
Restrict to an event kind.
.RE
.
.SS Mutations
All commands in this section prompt for confirmation before touching Beads
unless
.B \-\-yes
or
.B \-\-dry\-run
is given. See
.BR "MUTATION SAFETY" .
.TP
.BI "lb create" " title"
Create an issue.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-type " type"
Issue type. Default
.BR task .
.TP
.BI \-\-priority " n"
Priority 0\-4, where 0 is most urgent. Default 2.
.TP
.BI \-\-description " text"
Issue description.
.TP
.BI \-\-description\-file " path"
Read the description from a file. Overrides
.BR \-\-description .
.TP
.BI \-\-label " name"
Attach a label. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-assignee " actor"
Assign the new issue.
.TP
.BI \-\-parent " id"
Parent issue.
.TP
.BI \-\-metadata " key=value"
Attach metadata. Repeatable. A bare
.I key
with no
.B =
stores an empty value.
.RE
.TP
.BI "lb edit" " id"
Update fields on an issue. At least one field flag or
.B \-\-open\-in\-editor
is required; an edit that would change nothing is a usage error.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-title " text"
New title.
.TP
.BI \-\-description " text"
New description.
.TP
.BI \-\-description\-file " path"
Read the new description from a file.
.TP
.BI \-\-type " type"
New type.
.TP
.BI \-\-priority " n"
New priority, 0\-4.
.TP
.BI \-\-label " spec"
.BI add: name
adds a label and
.BI remove: name
removes one. A bare
.I name
is treated as
.BR add: .
Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-open\-in\-editor
Open the issue as YAML frontmatter in
.B $VISUAL
or
.BR $EDITOR ,
and apply whatever changed on save.
.RE
.TP
.BI "lb claim" " id"
Atomically claim an issue for the current actor. If the issue is already
assigned to somebody else, the confirmation prompt says so before you commit to
it.
.TP
.BI "lb unclaim" " id"
Release a claim, when the installed
.B bd
supports it. If it does not, the command exits with the capability code rather
than silently approximating the operation.
.TP
.BI "lb close" " id " [ reason ]
Close an issue. A reason is required and may be given either as trailing
arguments or with
.BR \-\-reason .
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-reason " text"
Close reason.
.RE
.TP
.BI "lb reopen" " id"
Reopen a closed issue.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-reason " text"
Reopen reason.
.RE
.TP
.BI "lb assign" " id " [ actor ]
Record responsibility without claiming.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-clear
Clear the assignee. Without this, an actor argument is required.
.RE
.
.SS Dependencies
.TP
.BI "lb dep add" " child parent"
Make
.I child
wait on
.IR parent .
Arguments are never reordered, and the relation is always printed explicitly in
the confirmation so the direction cannot be mistaken.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-type " relation"
Relation type. Default
.BR blocks .
.RE
.TP
.BI "lb dep remove" " child parent"
Remove a dependency edge.
.TP
.BI "lb dep list" " id"
List blockers and dependents of one issue.
.TP
.B lb dep validate
Report dependency cycles. Read-only: it never mutates anything.
.
.SS Memory
.TP
.B lb memory list
List durable project memories.
.TP
.BI "lb memory search" " query..."
Search memories.
.TP
.BI "lb memory add" " text..."
Remember a durable note. This is a mutation and confirms.
.TP
.BI "lb memory retire" " id"
Forget a memory. This is a mutation and confirms.
.TP
.B lb memory prime
Print the Beads workflow context block, suitable for feeding to an agent at the
start of a session.
.
.SS Sync
.TP
.B lb sync status
Read-only visibility into Beads and Dolt remote state. This is also what plain
.B lb sync
does.
.TP
.BR "lb sync pull" ", " "lb sync push"
Deferred from v1. Both exit with a usage error directing you to run
.B bd dolt pull
or
.B bd dolt push
yourself after inspecting
.BR "lb sync status" .
Mutating sync is deliberately not wrapped: it rewrites shared history, and
LazyBeads will not do that behind a confirmation prompt it designed.
.
.SS Diagnostics and shell integration
.TP
.B lb doctor
Diagnose tool, workspace, and operator health. Unlike every other command,
.B lb doctor
still runs and reports when workspace resolution itself failed, so it can
explain why nothing else works.
.RS
.PP
Checks include:
.BR bd " presence and version, JSON schema compatibility, workspace resolution,"
actor configuration, which configuration files were loaded, keybinding
collisions, editor availability, stale claims, dependency cycles, and sync
state.
.TP
.B \-\-fix
Write local configuration, the cache directory, and shell completion scripts.
It never mutates Beads and never edits your shell rc files; it prints the paths
it wrote and leaves sourcing to you.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Include per-check detail.
.RE
.TP
.BR "lb completion" " " { bash | zsh | fish | powershell }
Print a shell completion script on standard output. See
.BR "SHELL COMPLETION" .
.TP
.B lb man
Print this manual page in
.BR roff (7)
form on standard output. This is what
.B make install
pipes into the man directory.
.TP
.B lb version
Print the LazyBeads version.
.
.SS Interactive
.TP
.B lb tui
Start the full-screen interface.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-view " name"
Initial view:
.BR ready " (default), " focus ", " blocked ", " issues ", " activity ", " memory ", or " health .
.TP
.BI \-\-issue " id"
Open this issue in the detail view on startup.
.RE
.
.SH WORKSPACE RESOLUTION
The Beads workspace is resolved from the first of these that yields one:
.IP 1. 4
.B \-\-beads\-dir
.IP 2. 4
.B LB_BEADS_DIR
.IP 3. 4
.B workspace.beads_dir
in configuration
.IP 4. 4
discovery upward from
.B \-\-project
or, failing that, the current working directory
.PP
.B \-\-rig
selects among rigs when the resolved workspace exposes more than one.
Resolution failure is exit code 4, and the error names the directory that was
searched.
.
.SH ACTOR IDENTITY
The actor is the identity LazyBeads records on mutations and resolves for
.BR "\-\-assignee me" ,
.BR "lb focus" ,
and the "my active work" grouping. It is resolved from the first non-empty
value of:
.IP 1. 4
the
.B \-\-actor
flag
.IP 2. 4
the
.B LB_ACTOR
environment variable
.IP 3. 4
.B general.actor
in configuration
.IP 4. 4
.BR "git config user.name" ,
then
.BR "git config user.email" ,
when
.B general.use_git_identity
is true
.PP
With no actor configured,
.B lb status
and
.B lb doctor
raise a warning, and
.B \-\-assignee me
is a usage error. Mutations still work; they are simply recorded without an
attributed operator.
.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is TOML. Layers are merged lowest to highest:
.IP 1. 4
built-in defaults
.IP 2. 4
the user configuration file
.IP 3. 4
the project file
.RB ( .lazybeads.toml ,
discovered by walking upward from the starting directory to the filesystem
root)
.IP 4. 4
environment variables
.IP 5. 4
command-line flags
.PP
A missing file is not an error. An unreadable or malformed one is, and the
message always names the offending path.
.B lb doctor
lists every file that actually contributed.
.
.SS [general]
.TP
.B bd_binary
Path or name of the Beads executable. Default
.BR bd .
.TP
.B actor
Operator identity. See
.BR "ACTOR IDENTITY" .
.TP
.B color
.BR auto " (default), " always ", or " never .
.TP
.B default_view
Initial TUI view. Default
.BR ready .
.TP
.B confirm_mutations
Boolean, default
.BR true .
Setting it false disables the confirmation prompt for this workspace.
.TP
.B stale_after
Idle threshold used by
.BR "lb stale" .
Default
.BR 8h .
Must be positive.
.TP
.B refresh_interval
TUI auto-refresh interval. Default
.BR 30s .
Must be positive.
.TP
.B timeout
Per-invocation
.B bd
timeout. Default
.BR 30s .
Must be positive.
.TP
.B use_git_identity
Boolean. Fall back to the repository's git identity when no actor is otherwise
configured. Default false.
.
.SS [workspace]
.TP
.B project
Repository path to resolve from.
.TP
.B beads_dir
Explicit Beads directory.
.TP
.B rig
Rig name.
.TP
.B focus_parent
Epic or parent that
.B lb focus
treats as the current focus.
.TP
.B focus_labels
Array of labels that mark focused work; contributes
.B focus_weight
to ranking.
.TP
.B exclude_labels
Array of labels whose issues are hidden from ranked views.
.TP
.B ignore_issues
Array of issue ids to suppress entirely.
.
.SS [ranking]
Every weight is exposed here on purpose: no factor may influence a
recommendation invisibly.
.TP
.B strategy
.BR priority ", " leverage ", " age ", " balanced " (default), or " random .
.TP
.B priority_weight
Default 100.
.TP
.B leverage_weight
Default 15. Leverage counts the issues an issue directly unblocks.
.TP
.B age_weight
Default 1.
.TP
.B focus_weight
Default 25. Applied to issues matching
.B workspace.focus_parent
or
.BR workspace.focus_labels .
.TP
.B recently_unblocked_weight
Default 10. Applies only when an issue's update time is later than its creation
time, that is, when it was genuinely released by a later unblocking rather than
merely newly filed.
.TP
.B complexity_penalty_weight
Default 0.
.TP
.B max_graph_depth
Default 8. Bounds
.B lb why
and
.BR "lb graph" .
.TP
.B max_graph_nodes
Default 500. Traversal that hits this bound reports truncation rather than
silently returning a partial graph.
.
.SS [tui]
.TP
.B mouse
Enable mouse support. Default false.
.TP
.B ascii
Use ASCII glyphs. Default false.
.TP
.B compact
Denser rows. Default false.
.TP
.B show_descriptions
Show descriptions in the preview pane. Default true.
.TP
.B reduced_motion
Suppress animation and spinners. Default false.
.
.SS [keys]
.TP
.B layout
.BR logical " (default) or " physical .
.TP
.BR global ", " list ", " detail
Tables mapping an action name to an array of key strings, overriding the
built-in bindings for that scope. Collisions are reported by
.BR "lb doctor" .
.
.SS [aliases]
A table of user-defined command aliases.
.
.SS Example
.RS 4
.nf
[general]
actor = "leslie"
use_git_identity = true
stale_after = "2d"

[workspace]
focus_parent = "lb-epic-1"
exclude_labels = ["wontfix", "icebox"]

[ranking]
strategy = "balanced"
leverage_weight = 25
max_graph_depth = 6

[tui]
show_descriptions = true
.fi
.RE
.
.SH DURATION SYNTAX
Durations accept Go syntax
.RB ( 300ms ", " 90s ", " 5m ", " 2h ,
and combinations such as
.BR 1h30m ),
plus two extensions:
.B d
for days and
.B w
for weeks
.RB ( 2d ", " 3w ).
A bare number is read as seconds, so
.B 30
and
.B 30s
are the same.
.PP
The
.BR \-\-since " and " \-\-recent
flags additionally accept the literal
.BR today ,
meaning "since local midnight".
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LB_ACTOR
Operator identity. Overrides configuration; overridden by
.BR \-\-actor .
.TP
.B LB_BD_BIN
Path to the
.B bd
executable.
.TP
.B LB_COLOR
Color mode.
.TP
.B LB_PROJECT
Repository path to resolve from.
.TP
.B LB_BEADS_DIR
Explicit Beads directory.
.TP
.B LB_RIG
Rig name.
.TP
.B LB_TIMEOUT
Per-invocation timeout. An unparseable value is ignored rather than fatal.
.TP
.B LB_NO_CONFIRM
Truthy
.RB ( 1 ", " true ", " yes ", " on )
disables mutation confirmation. This is deliberately environment-only: a
project configuration file must never be able to silently disable confirmation
for a repository you just cloned. When it is set and the session is
interactive,
.B lb
warns before proceeding anyway.
.TP
.B LB_CONFIG
Override the user configuration file path entirely.
.TP
.BR LB_CACHE_DIR ", " LB_DATA_DIR
Override the cache and data directories.
.TP
.BR VISUAL ", " EDITOR
Editor used by
.BR "lb edit \-\-open\-in\-editor" .
.B VISUAL
is preferred. The value may carry arguments, for example
.BR "code \-w" ;
it is split on whitespace and executed as an argument vector, never through a
shell.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME
Consulted on Linux and other Unix systems for the paths under
.BR FILES .
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .lazybeads.toml
Project configuration, discovered by walking upward from the starting
directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/lazybeads/config.toml
User configuration on Linux and Unix
.RB ( $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lazybeads/config.toml
when set).
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/lazybeads/config.toml
User configuration on macOS.
.TP
.I %AppData%\eLazybeads\econfig.toml
User configuration on Windows.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/lazybeads/completions/
Completion scripts written by
.BR "lb doctor \-\-fix" .
On macOS this is
.IR "~/Library/Application Support/lazybeads/completions/" .
.TP
.I ~/.cache/lazybeads/
Cache directory. On macOS,
.IR ~/Library/Caches/lazybeads/ .
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error not covered by a more specific code.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown command or flag, bad argument count, invalid value.
.TP
.B 3
.B bd
is unavailable: not on
.BR PATH ,
not executable, or it failed to start.
.TP
.B 4
Workspace could not be resolved.
.TP
.B 5
Schema mismatch: the
.B bd
output could not be decoded against the expected contract.
.TP
.B 6
Capability missing: the installed
.B bd
does not support the requested operation. LazyBeads reports this rather than
approximating the operation with something else.
.TP
.B 7
Mutation rejected by Beads.
.TP
.B 8
Confirmation declined by the operator.
.TP
.B 9
Timed out.
.TP
.B 10
Internal invariant violated. This is a bug; please report it.
.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
With
.BR \-\-json " or " "\-\-format json" ,
every successful command emits one envelope:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "command": "ready",
  "workspace": { "root_path": "/path/to/repo", "rig": null },
  "data": { },
  "warnings": [],
  "generated_at": "2026-09-11T09:00:00Z"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Failures emit an error envelope instead, on standard output, alongside the
exit code:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "command": "claim",
  "error": {
    "code": "capability",
    "message": "...",
    "hint": "...",
    "upstream_stderr": null
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B schema_version
is 1. Adding fields is backward compatible; renaming or removing one increments
the version. Scripts should key off
.B error.code
and the exit status, not off message text.
.B upstream_stderr
carries the captured
.B bd
stderr when there was any.
.PP
.B \-\-format jsonl
emits one JSON object per line for streaming consumers.
.
.SH MUTATION SAFETY
Every mutation follows the same path: LazyBeads builds the exact
.B bd
argument vector, shows it to you, and only then runs it.
.PP
The confirmation prompt names the workspace, the issue id and title, the full
command, and any warnings, for example that the issue is already claimed by
somebody else:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[y] Confirm  [n] Cancel  [v] View raw command:
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B v
prints the argument vector and asks again. Declining exits 8.
.PP
Confirmation is skipped when
.B \-\-yes
is given, when
.B \-\-dry\-run
is given (nothing is executed at all), or when it has been disabled through
.B general.confirm_mutations
or
.BR LB_NO_CONFIRM .
In a non-interactive context with none of those, a mutation is refused with a
usage error rather than proceeding unattended.
.PP
Arguments are passed to
.B bd
as a vector. No shell is involved at any point, so issue titles, labels, and
reasons containing shell metacharacters are safe. All text originating from
Beads is sanitised of control sequences before being written to the terminal.
.
.SH INTERACTIVE INTERFACE
.B lb tui
(or plain
.B lb
on a terminal) opens a tiled console: a stats header, context tabs, a list
panel beside a live preview, and a keybinding bar. Below roughly 100 columns
the preview pane hides itself.
.
.SS Keys
.TP
.BR j ", " k ", arrows"
Move.
.TP
.B tab
Move focus between the list and the preview pane. With the preview focused,
the motion keys scroll it.
.TP
.BR ctrl+d ", " ctrl+u ", " pgdn ", " pgup
Half-page down and up.
.TP
.BR G ", " end ", " home
Last and first item.
.TP
.B enter
Open the issue detail view.
.TP
.B esc
Back, clear the filter, or cancel an overlay.
.TP
.B q
Back; quit at the top level.
.TP
.BR r ", " f ", " b ", " i ", " a ", " m ", " h
Switch to Ready, Focus, Blocked, Issues, Activity, Memory, or Health.
.TP
.B g
Dependency graph for the selected issue.
.TP
.BR c ", " u ", " x ", " n
Claim, unclaim, close, create. All confirm; close asks for a reason first.
.TP
.B /
Filter. See
.BR "Filter grammar" .
.TP
.BR [ ", " ]
Cycle the status filter forward and backward in the Issues view:
open, in_progress, blocked, deferred, closed, and back to all.
.TP
.B :
Command palette.
.TP
.B R
Refresh.
.TP
.B ?
Help overlay.
.TP
.BR y ", " Y
Copy the selected issue id, or
.BI "lb show " id ,
to the system clipboard. Native clipboard tools are used where available, with
an OSC 52 escape fallback so it also works over SSH.
.
.SS Filter grammar
The
.B /
overlay accepts a bare status word
.RB ( open ", " closed ", " in_progress ", " blocked ", " deferred ),
the same word prefixed with
.BR status: " or " is: ,
or any other text, which becomes a substring match across id, title, status,
and labels. Hyphens and underscores are interchangeable, and matching is
case-insensitive.
.
.SS Command palette
The
.B :
overlay accepts
.BR ready ", " focus ", " blocked ", " issues ", " activity ", " memory ", "
.BR health " (also " doctor " or " status ), " help ", " claim ", " refresh ", and"
.BR quit " (or " q ).
Commands match on prefix.
.PP
The TUI calls exactly the same service layer as the command line. There is no
behaviour available in one and not the other, and mutations confirm in both.
.
.SH SHELL COMPLETION
.B lb completion
writes a script to standard output:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lb completion bash > /usr/local/etc/bash_completion.d/lb
lb completion zsh  > "${fpath[1]}/_lb"
lb completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/lb.fish
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B make install
installs all three under the chosen prefix.
.B lb doctor \-\-fix
writes them into the user data directory instead and tells you where; it does
not edit rc files on your behalf.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Find something to work on, and understand the choice:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lb next \-\-verbose
lb why lb\-42
.fi
.RE
.PP
Claim it and close it later with a reason:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lb claim lb\-42
lb close lb\-42 "fixed in 7886551; regression test added"
.fi
.RE
.PP
See what the command would be, without running it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lb close lb\-42 \-\-reason done \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Unattended use in a script:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lb ready \-\-json \-\-priority\-max 1 | jq \-r '.data.issues[].id'
lb claim lb\-42 \-\-yes \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
What is blocking the most work:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lb blocked \-\-group\-by blocker
lb graph lb\-7 \-\-direction dependents \-\-format dot | dot \-Tpng > deps.png
.fi
.RE
.PP
Who is sitting on stale claims:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lb stale \-\-since 3d \-\-claimed\-only
lb activity \-\-since today \-\-actor leslie
.fi
.RE
.PP
Diagnose an installation:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
lb doctor \-\-verbose
lb doctor \-\-fix
lb \-\-debug status
.fi
.RE
.
